Water features - Water features: There are no influencing water features on this site. Soil features - Soil features: This site occurs on deep soils. The dry surface layer color is typically reddish brown to brown and surface textures range from gravelly and cobbly loams to very cobbly fine sandy loams. These soils are well developed, well drained, and have low to moderate water holding capacities. Soil temperature regime is mesic and moisture regime is ustic aridic (torric). Erosion potential of soils on reference state sites typically depends on surface rock fragments. Sites with greater than 50% rock fragments have lower wind and water erosion potentials than sites with less than 50% surface rock fragments. Biological crust cover is characterized as crustless with the possible occurrence of light cyanobacteria and/or isolated lichen and moss pinnacles. This site has been used in the following soils surveys and has been correlated to the following components: UT631 - Henry Mountains - Stormitt;
UT633 - Canyonlands Area - Moab;
